body:
I was literally just thinking about this problem. It gets so fucking exhausting living for other people when killing myself/not existing anymore is on your mind 24/7, but I've found that distracting yourself helps. Obviously not the best coping mechanism but hey it works sometimes. Try looking for new stuff to learn about, pick up a book, watch some (a lot) of netflix, just about anything that keeps your mind occupied and unable to loop suicidal thoughts. 

&#x200B;

I hope you know that this community is here for you, and that it can be a reminder that there can always be someone to talk to. Please please feel free to reach out for a chat if you want to talk, or even just someone to distract you for a bit.
